### 13. Acceptance Criteria

The application is ready for a controlled pilot only when:

1. An authorized officer can register a physical file and assign a storage location.
2. Staff can search for a permitted file and see its correct current location.
3. An employee can submit a request and follow its status.
4. An authorized manager can approve or reject a request.
5. An archive officer can record a verified physical handover.
6. The file's current holder and status update consistently.
7. A return updates the holder, storage location, and request status.
8. Every movement is preserved in the history.
9. Concurrent issue attempts cannot assign the same file twice.
10. Unauthorized users cannot access restricted document metadata.
11. Audit events are protected from ordinary application modifications.
12. Overdue and missing-file reports use actual database records.
13. English and Amharic interfaces work throughout the application.
14. Automated tests pass, and backup restoration has been tested.
15. Production setup and operational documentation are complete.

